import lib/process.dl

function the stress process test interpreter:
    execute:
        return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set length to 262144
set input to a new string buffer containing length bytes
set position to 0
loop while position < length:
    store 73 as a byte into the data of input at position
    set position to position + 1

set command to a process command for the stress process test interpreter
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import sys\nsize=262144\nsys.stdout.write('O'*size); sys.stdout.flush()\nsys.stderr.write('E'*size); sys.stderr.flush()\ndata=sys.stdin.buffer.read()\nsys.stdout.write(str(len(data)))" as an argument to command
run command using input and set result to it

print whether result was launched as a line
print whether result succeeded as a line
print result's exit code as a line
print whether (result's standard output's length = length + 6) as a line
print whether (the character at 0 in result's standard output = 79) as a line
print whether (the character at (length - 1) in result's standard output = 79) as a line
print whether (the substring of result's standard output from length spanning 6 bytes = "262144") as a line
print whether (result's standard error's length = length) as a line
print whether (the character at 0 in result's standard error = 69) as a line
print whether (the character at (length - 1) in result's standard error = 69) as a line
